# Squeezelite arguments for the HiFi Player appliance.
# -v  enables the visualizer shared-memory export (/dev/shm/squeezelite-*)
#     which the VU-meter daemon reads. DO NOT remove -v or the VU meter stops working.
# -D  enables DSD playback. Without it squeezelite downconverts DSD to PCM; with it
#     DSD is passed bit-perfect to a DSD-capable DAC via DoP (DSD over PCM).
# -s 127.0.0.1  points to the local Lyrion Music Server. Settings → Multiroom
#               can rewrite this to another Osmium device's IP ("follow" mode)
#               so this player joins that device's LMS for multiroom grouping
#               (api_server.py set_lms_role / GET+POST /lms_role).
# -M OsmiumSound  overrides the model name squeezelite declares to Lyrion in its
#               SlimProto handshake (ModelName=, default "SqueezeLite"): it is what
#               the server shows under Settings > Player > Information and
#               writes in its logs, so an Osmium unit is recognisable there and
#               tellable apart from any other squeezelite on the same LAN. Purely
#               cosmetic/diagnostic: the machine-readable Model=squeezelite field is
#               hardcoded in the binary and untouched by -M, so plugins that key off
#               it keep working. Unlike -n (renamable per device) this stays fixed.
# -o default    uses the ALSA default device. The UI wizard rewrites this to a
#               specific DAC. It uses the stable card *name*, e.g.
#               -o hw:CARD=D50s,DEV=0  (NOT -o hw:1,0 — card numbers can change
#               across reboots, the CARD= name does not). Run `aplay -l` to list.
ARGS='-o default -D -v -C 5 -s 127.0.0.1 -n OsmiumSound -M OsmiumSound'
